WEBVTT

00:00:01.106 --> 00:00:05.966
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:12.346
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:23.996 --> 00:00:29.326
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:34.766
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.936 --> 00:00:41.206
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.746 --> 00:00:46.876
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.286 --> 00:00:50.806
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:55.986
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.626 --> 00:01:01.116
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.696 --> 00:01:08.656
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.736 --> 00:01:14.636
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tsuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:21.276
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.546 --> 00:01:27.486
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:02:01.986 --> 00:02:03.546
So you're all right.

00:02:04.096 --> 00:02:06.686
What happened to your outfit?

00:02:06.756 --> 00:02:08.096
I don't know.

00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:11.426
I guess that's what it means
to be initialized.

00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:13.926
Uh, nothing.

00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:15.636
I'm glad you're safe.

00:02:17.376 --> 00:02:18.336
Haseo!

00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:20.796
Phyllo is not coming back.

00:02:20.876 --> 00:02:21.666
Huh?

00:02:21.746 --> 00:02:23.436
He didn't actually quit.

00:02:24.446 --> 00:02:26.846
But I guess it's the same thing.

00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:28.346
I don't get it.

00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:30.436
We have no privacy here.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:31.986
Let's go somewhere else.

00:02:32.286 --> 00:02:33.846
I have something to tell you.

00:02:37.926 --> 00:02:38.946
Shino...

00:02:39.896 --> 00:02:41.056
It's starting now.

00:02:47.536 --> 00:02:50.336
I need to go tell Shino.

00:02:52.206 --> 00:02:53.266
Huh?

00:02:54.576 --> 00:02:55.666
Oh well.

00:03:11.596 --> 00:03:12.616
No way.

00:03:13.356 --> 00:03:15.986
Phyllo was in the game
the whole time.

00:03:16.366 --> 00:03:18.156
He never did anything...

00:03:18.236 --> 00:03:19.896
...except hang out at Mac Anu.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.936
That's right.

00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:25.596
He was always there,
worried about you until the end.

00:03:25.676 --> 00:03:26.636
About me?

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.266
At the very end...

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.576
...Phyllo asked me to
look out for you.

00:03:34.076 --> 00:03:35.476
I don't understand.

00:03:35.546 --> 00:03:36.676
Really?

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.206
Knowing he had cancer with
only eight months left to live...

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.726
...how could he continue to
calmly play this game?

00:03:43.586 --> 00:03:45.926
And he was worrying about me?

00:03:46.756 --> 00:03:49.026
He should have been
worrying about himself!

00:03:49.096 --> 00:03:50.686
Of course he was.

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:53.666
Phyllo...

00:03:56.506 --> 00:03:59.766
Phyllo had taken care of
all his affairs...

00:03:59.836 --> 00:04:02.006
...and he was still
worried about you.

00:04:02.246 --> 00:04:03.206
But...

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:09.346
What would you do if you were
told you had eight months to live?

00:04:09.646 --> 00:04:10.676
What?

00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:13.906
Would you be desperate?
Depressed?

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.316
Or would you frantically try to
achieve something...

00:04:17.386 --> 00:04:19.156
...so you could leave a legacy?

00:04:19.226 --> 00:04:22.056
Those are the only possibilities
we can imagine.

00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:24.196
Yeah, I guess.

00:04:24.866 --> 00:04:27.236
Phyllo didn't choose any of those.

00:04:29.506 --> 00:04:30.966
In his last days...

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:34.566
...he wanted to live calmly,
as though nothing had changed.

00:04:35.206 --> 00:04:37.736
That was how he lived his life.

00:04:37.816 --> 00:04:39.106
Calmly, huh?

00:04:39.346 --> 00:04:42.376
"I'm aware I will be
dying soon..."

00:04:42.446 --> 00:04:45.616
"...but you, who don't have to
worry about such things..."

00:04:45.686 --> 00:04:47.746
"...could die the next day
in an accident."

00:04:48.156 --> 00:04:52.456
"In that moment, who will be
the one to have regrets?"

00:04:53.896 --> 00:04:55.956
Phyllo said that with a chuckle.

00:04:59.336 --> 00:05:02.666
He told me that you're trying to do
too much by yourself.

00:05:04.206 --> 00:05:07.696
He also said he was overly harsh,
and he regretted that.

00:05:11.876 --> 00:05:15.676
I don't really remember
anything he said.

00:05:16.386 --> 00:05:19.376
I shrugged him off as a nuisance.
That's all.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:27.956
"Whatever happens, never let go
of what you believe in."

00:05:30.126 --> 00:05:31.926
That's Phyllo's message to you.

00:05:33.536 --> 00:05:35.156
I already know that.

00:05:43.106 --> 00:05:44.266
Master Yata...

00:05:44.346 --> 00:05:46.836
I've found the unidentified phenomena.

00:05:53.756 --> 00:05:54.816
Where's Kuhn?

00:05:54.886 --> 00:05:56.616
I believe he's in the main room.

00:05:56.686 --> 00:05:58.386
Destroy the target.

00:05:58.456 --> 00:06:00.726
If possible, get a sample.

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.086
Yes.

00:06:10.566 --> 00:06:13.406
What's up, all of a sudden?
Coming all this way.

00:06:13.476 --> 00:06:15.536
Haseo's back.

00:06:15.606 --> 00:06:16.576
I know.

00:06:16.646 --> 00:06:18.876
- Don't you want to see him?
- Why would I?

00:06:18.946 --> 00:06:20.706
What do you mean, why?

00:06:21.386 --> 00:06:23.006
I guess I can understand.

00:06:23.086 --> 00:06:26.076
If he logged in
that means he's okay, right?

00:06:26.516 --> 00:06:30.216
Maintain a moderate distance.
That's one of my principles.

00:06:30.286 --> 00:06:32.586
So you're a spectator by nature?

00:06:32.656 --> 00:06:35.026
I don't want to get burned
by getting involved.

00:06:35.096 --> 00:06:37.286
That depends on who
you're getting involved with.

00:06:37.366 --> 00:06:40.336
You tend to associate
with the wrong people...

00:06:40.396 --> 00:06:42.296
...and find yourself
in sticky situations.

00:06:42.366 --> 00:06:43.666
- Right?
- Huh?

00:06:45.176 --> 00:06:47.166
Well, I won't deny it.

00:06:47.536 --> 00:06:49.766
Haseo's like Chinese food.

00:06:49.846 --> 00:06:50.746
What?

00:06:50.806 --> 00:06:53.646
You get full just by smelling
the aroma.

00:06:53.716 --> 00:06:55.006
It's kind of like that.

00:06:55.386 --> 00:06:57.746
But that enticing aroma
makes you hungry.

00:06:57.816 --> 00:06:59.186
I don't get bored of watching.

00:06:59.256 --> 00:07:01.546
You're fine with just smelling
and looking?

00:07:01.626 --> 00:07:03.646
Yeah. It's way more fun.

00:07:07.096 --> 00:07:08.556
Are you in the bathroom?

00:07:09.226 --> 00:07:10.956
As long as you're around...

00:07:11.036 --> 00:07:13.466
...I'm sure I don't have to
worry about anything.

00:07:13.536 --> 00:07:14.936
Are you quitting again?

00:07:15.006 --> 00:07:17.736
We can play this game
because there is real life.

00:07:17.806 --> 00:07:19.936
There are other things
I have to take care of.

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:22.376
I don't know what you're up to...

00:07:22.446 --> 00:07:24.936
...but I'm sure you'll be fine, Tawaraya.

00:07:25.016 --> 00:07:27.446
Leave things to me,
and go do what you have to.

00:07:28.546 --> 00:07:29.776
That's my plan.

00:07:31.256 --> 00:07:32.216
Thanks!

00:07:46.366 --> 00:07:49.596
First you call up the Avatar,
and then attack.

00:07:49.666 --> 00:07:53.036
If you don't think you can do it,
withdraw your Avatar...

00:07:53.106 --> 00:07:54.576
...and I'll deal with it.

00:07:54.646 --> 00:07:57.666
I've done this before.
I know what I'm doing.

00:08:01.886 --> 00:08:03.006
Hey!

00:08:04.486 --> 00:08:06.246
What is this?!

00:08:11.396 --> 00:08:12.446
Let's do it.

00:08:12.526 --> 00:08:13.546
Wait!

00:08:14.966 --> 00:08:17.126
There's something in the bug hole.

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:18.526
Your instructions, Master Yata?

00:08:20.096 --> 00:08:23.366
I'd like to see what comes out of it.

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:37.446
It's imitating an active life form?

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:38.646
Master Yata!

00:08:43.226 --> 00:08:44.216
Your instructions?!

00:08:44.286 --> 00:08:45.226
That's enough.

00:08:45.296 --> 00:08:46.316
Destroy it.

00:08:46.496 --> 00:08:47.456
Yes!

00:08:52.366 --> 00:08:54.496
Don't chicken out now!
Let's go!

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:55.626
All right!

00:09:19.756 --> 00:09:23.956
I really can't
believe you're dead, Phyllo.

00:09:25.836 --> 00:09:27.996
I can't accept that you're gone.

00:09:29.036 --> 00:09:30.026
Why?

00:09:46.756 --> 00:09:50.776
Forget about getting a sample.
That thing was a beast.

00:09:51.726 --> 00:09:53.586
Let's just go back for now.

00:09:53.656 --> 00:09:54.686
Yeah.

00:09:54.996 --> 00:09:57.966
If that kind of thing starts popping
up all over the game...

00:09:59.096 --> 00:10:00.926
...this world will be destroyed.

00:10:22.386 --> 00:10:25.486
Are you the Haseo they
talked about in the forums?

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:29.186
I've been through a lot too.

00:10:30.966 --> 00:10:33.866
I have a feeling you and I
could become friends.

00:10:35.136 --> 00:10:36.196
Get lost.

00:10:36.266 --> 00:10:37.466
I see.

00:10:38.076 --> 00:10:40.836
Part of my name means "man".

00:10:41.136 --> 00:10:43.666
We have a lot in common.

00:10:44.006 --> 00:10:46.136
Maybe we'll meet again sometime.

00:10:46.446 --> 00:10:47.746
I'm not interested.

00:10:50.486 --> 00:10:53.546
That's the story.
You guys keep playing as usual.

00:10:55.356 --> 00:10:56.756
Ta-daa!

00:10:58.296 --> 00:11:00.416
We started an information service!

00:11:00.496 --> 00:11:02.686
- Information service?!
- That's right.

00:11:02.766 --> 00:11:03.816
An information service.

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:07.526
We figured we'd be better off
dealing in information.

00:11:07.596 --> 00:11:08.936
You guys...

00:11:09.006 --> 00:11:12.196
So, you go and study hard.

00:11:12.276 --> 00:11:14.506
Come back any time
if you're lonely.

00:11:14.576 --> 00:11:15.666
Look, you...

00:11:15.746 --> 00:11:18.106
There he is! Hey, Tohta!

00:11:19.776 --> 00:11:21.876
Hi! What's going on, Tabby?

00:11:22.116 --> 00:11:23.176
I'm sorry.

00:11:23.246 --> 00:11:24.186
For what?

00:11:24.246 --> 00:11:27.706
I feel bad that I disbanded
the guild you helped me start.

00:11:27.786 --> 00:11:29.186
That doesn't matter.

00:11:29.256 --> 00:11:30.986
It seems like you've settled down.

00:11:31.056 --> 00:11:31.926
Yeah!

00:11:31.996 --> 00:11:33.186
And these...

00:11:33.726 --> 00:11:35.426
I won't need them anymore.

00:11:35.526 --> 00:11:36.726
Are you quitting?

00:11:36.866 --> 00:11:38.986
I have a goal in real life now.

00:11:39.236 --> 00:11:41.826
As much as I'd like
to take them...

00:11:41.906 --> 00:11:43.396
...I'm quitting as well.

00:11:44.166 --> 00:11:46.226
I've also got my real life, too.

00:11:46.306 --> 00:11:48.776
- Would you like us to take them?
- Huh?

00:11:48.846 --> 00:11:51.276
Because we'll always be here.

00:11:52.516 --> 00:11:54.846
They're not really for sale.

00:11:55.786 --> 00:11:57.976
These guys are my successors.

00:11:58.056 --> 00:11:59.316
They won't sell these.

00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:00.406
Really?

00:12:00.486 --> 00:12:02.076
Yeah, don't worry about it.

00:12:02.256 --> 00:12:03.346
Okay!

00:12:03.426 --> 00:12:06.086
I'll be back after I achieve my goal!

00:12:06.996 --> 00:12:08.426
Sure! Come again!

00:12:09.726 --> 00:12:11.356
Oh boy...

00:12:27.316 --> 00:12:29.946
I guess I'm alone then.

00:12:38.456 --> 00:12:39.786
You want to go back?

00:12:41.566 --> 00:12:43.726
You can't turn back time.

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:47.896
After all those incidents, it's no wonder
you have no energy left in you.

00:12:48.166 --> 00:12:49.596
That's not it.

00:12:50.366 --> 00:12:52.206
Is it sad being lonely?

00:12:55.006 --> 00:12:57.996
Look around and you'll see
a lot of people are that way.

00:12:58.076 --> 00:13:00.066
I mean, just look at me!

00:13:00.146 --> 00:13:01.206
You, too?

00:13:05.356 --> 00:13:07.406
Before there was TV...

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:10.756
...people used to watch
the fireplace or gaze at candles.

00:13:13.396 --> 00:13:15.756
Where do you get this from?

00:13:15.826 --> 00:13:19.056
People need visual stimulation
from things that move.

00:13:19.136 --> 00:13:19.926
What?

00:13:19.996 --> 00:13:21.366
Don't you get it?

00:13:21.436 --> 00:13:22.796
I don't.

00:13:22.866 --> 00:13:25.926
There are people who watch
and care about you.

00:13:26.006 --> 00:13:27.976
So go and make your move already!

00:13:28.546 --> 00:13:29.906
It's all about you, huh?

00:13:30.576 --> 00:13:31.566
Yup.

00:13:32.916 --> 00:13:35.606
I'm always on the move.

00:13:37.546 --> 00:13:40.676
Hey, how would you like to
heal PCs with me?

00:13:41.056 --> 00:13:41.746
Huh?

00:13:41.826 --> 00:13:46.086
In a game like this, people need
to be healed, don't you think?

00:13:46.356 --> 00:13:47.756
- Right?
- Come on!

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.456
Quit messing around!

00:13:49.526 --> 00:13:51.556
W-Wait!

00:13:51.636 --> 00:13:53.256
She's hot!

00:13:53.636 --> 00:13:55.826
Wait!

00:13:55.906 --> 00:13:56.956
Creep.

00:14:01.676 --> 00:14:02.666
Haseo?

00:14:03.076 --> 00:14:05.476
Haseo! Haseo!

00:14:06.176 --> 00:14:07.836
Haseo!

00:14:08.116 --> 00:14:09.176
Welcome back!

00:14:10.216 --> 00:14:11.686
Get off me!

00:14:11.756 --> 00:14:13.716
But I'm so happy you're back!

00:14:14.156 --> 00:14:15.446
You're annoying!

00:14:16.526 --> 00:14:18.586
It's you! It really is you!

00:14:19.326 --> 00:14:20.916
It's totally you!

00:14:21.666 --> 00:14:23.426
Haseo!

00:14:38.916 --> 00:14:39.966
You're lying.

00:14:40.046 --> 00:14:41.776
Why would I lie?

00:14:42.416 --> 00:14:43.406
I'm sorry.

00:14:43.946 --> 00:14:45.146
But...

00:14:46.956 --> 00:14:49.516
Why didn't he tell me?

00:14:49.586 --> 00:14:51.926
We always talked a lot.

00:14:52.356 --> 00:14:53.586
Yeah.

00:14:54.556 --> 00:14:57.326
Well it's not exactly something
to talk about.

00:14:58.066 --> 00:15:00.156
Phyllo is mature, after all.

00:15:06.606 --> 00:15:07.666
You know what?

00:15:10.046 --> 00:15:11.336
Never mind.

00:15:16.516 --> 00:15:17.886
I'm going.

00:15:18.156 --> 00:15:19.486
Where to?

00:15:19.556 --> 00:15:20.846
I don't know.

00:15:20.916 --> 00:15:22.516
I just...

00:15:22.886 --> 00:15:25.186
...can't be standing still.

00:15:25.726 --> 00:15:29.126
Are you going out to
kill Player Killers again?

00:15:30.366 --> 00:15:31.526
No way.

00:15:32.936 --> 00:15:35.906
There's no use
in doing the same thing.

00:15:36.106 --> 00:15:37.126
I see.

00:15:37.506 --> 00:15:39.406
Are you going to keep
playing the game?

00:15:39.476 --> 00:15:42.836
Even though you've been initialized?

00:15:42.906 --> 00:15:45.806
I can't think of any other way
to go on.

00:15:45.876 --> 00:15:46.846
Haseo...

00:15:47.846 --> 00:15:51.076
I just know
that you're the only one, Haseo...

00:15:51.146 --> 00:15:53.246
...who can save Shino.

00:15:55.026 --> 00:15:56.356
Not on my own.

00:15:58.196 --> 00:15:59.526
You're right.

00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:04.296
I've been thinking of
becoming a nurse!

00:16:04.726 --> 00:16:05.886
That's great.

00:16:05.966 --> 00:16:08.226
The way I see it is...

00:16:08.306 --> 00:16:11.296
...I'd be better off helping Shino
in the real world.

00:16:11.366 --> 00:16:13.236
How many years will it take?

00:16:13.836 --> 00:16:14.966
Uh, right...

00:16:15.046 --> 00:16:17.836
I'd already save her before that.

00:16:18.246 --> 00:16:20.806
But, if you can't do it...

00:16:22.246 --> 00:16:23.276
You know what?

00:16:23.346 --> 00:16:26.476
So don't be doing anything
reckless on your own.

00:16:26.556 --> 00:16:28.816
If you can't do it, I will.

00:16:28.886 --> 00:16:30.546
What're you saying?

00:16:33.056 --> 00:16:34.956
I like you, Haseo!

00:16:36.226 --> 00:16:40.856
I'm going to do my best
for my sake and study really hard.

00:16:40.936 --> 00:16:41.896
That's why...

00:16:42.506 --> 00:16:45.956
That's why you need to do
your best for your sake!

00:16:46.636 --> 00:16:47.606
Yeah.

00:16:50.046 --> 00:16:51.166
Of course!

00:16:59.356 --> 00:17:00.846
The time has come.

00:17:00.916 --> 00:17:02.516
What do you mean?

00:17:02.586 --> 00:17:04.526
As the Raven guild...

00:17:04.926 --> 00:17:07.756
As players who possess
the Factor...

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:09.816
...let's make contact with Haseo.

00:17:09.896 --> 00:17:11.416
You can leave it to me.

00:17:11.666 --> 00:17:12.926
And...

00:17:13.496 --> 00:17:15.726
...we need a name for this.

00:17:16.236 --> 00:17:17.296
A name?

00:17:17.366 --> 00:17:20.536
The characteristics
will be defined by the name.

00:17:20.906 --> 00:17:24.276
So, we must be careful
of what we label it.

00:17:24.846 --> 00:17:25.816
Yes.

00:17:28.516 --> 00:17:29.846
A. I.

00:17:29.916 --> 00:17:31.406
Artificial Intelligence.

00:17:31.486 --> 00:17:33.456
It seems the
unidentified phenomenon...

00:17:33.516 --> 00:17:36.486
...is the outcome of an uncontrolled,
abnormal A. I...

00:17:36.556 --> 00:17:39.486
...that originated
from the realms of the Net.

00:17:39.826 --> 00:17:40.796
Therefore...

00:17:40.996 --> 00:17:43.656
...we'll refer to this Artificial
Intelligence Data Anomaly...

00:17:44.966 --> 00:17:46.796
